//? Title: Exponential Backoff: Windows, Jitter and Cumulative Waiting
//? Subtitle: Checked finite retry calculations, the original seeded stream and synchronisation controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Several clients can fail together and then repeat their requests together,
creating bursts even when each client waits longer between retries. Capped
exponential windows bound each wait, while jitter spreads chosen delays within
those windows. We inspect a four-step example, preserve the original eight
seeded delays, and compare repeated seeds with distinct seeded clients.
Native C++ records expose actual windows, variates, delays and cumulative idle
waits. The scalar calculation handles every nonnegative int index without a
retry loop or intermediate floating overflow. These calculations neither send
requests nor determine whether retrying an operation is appropriate.
)

\toc

> Four windows, four waits, four different retry offsets

With base one and cap five, the first four windows are 1,2,4,5.
Apply explicit unit variates 0.25,0.5,0.75,1 to obtain waits
0.25,1,3,5. Adding these gives cumulative idle offsets
0.25,1.25,4.25,9.25. A window is a maximum for one wait; an offset
is the sum of waits so far. Request execution time is excluded.

The API numbers k from zero: k=0 is the wait before the first retry,
following the original failed operation. It accepts finite nonnegative
base/cap in one common caller-selected time unit. The explicit jitter
function retains u=1 for compatibility, although a generated uniform
variate comes from [0,1). Rounding at very small windows can still put
a product on a window endpoint.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/backoff_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto s=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_schedule(4,1,5,{.25,.5,.75,1});
  std::print("| k | actual window | actual u | actual delay | cumulative idle wait | capped | scaled with ldexp |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(56,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.6;box.height=2.2;box.font_size=22;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<s.steps.size();++i){const auto& r=s.steps[i];std::print("| {} | {:.2f} | {:.2f} | {:.2f} | {:.2f} | {} | {} |\n",r.attempt,r.window,r.u,r.delay,s.retry_times[i],r.capped,r.scaled);
    box.fill=r.capped?dm::graphics::RGB{254,215,170}:dm::graphics::RGB{191,219,254};g.node(std::to_string(i),{5.*i,0},std::format("k = {}\nwindow {:.2f}\nu {:.2f}\nwait {:.2f}",r.attempt,r.window,r.u,r.delay),box).text({5.*i,-2},std::format("offset {:.2f}",s.retry_times[i]),22);if(i)g.edge(std::to_string(i-1),std::to_string(i),"then");}
  g.text({7.5,3.5},"Actual capped windows and chosen waits",26).text({7.5,-3.7},std::format("Cumulative idle wait: {:.2f}; request duration excluded",s.total_delay),23).save_svg("build/backoff_tiny.svg");
  if(s.retry_times!=std::vector<double>{.25,1.25,4.25,9.25})throw std::runtime_error("tiny idle-offset identity failed");
}
