> Sum idle waits without confusing them with service completion

With no cap yet active, the deterministic offset after waits zero through
k is b(2^(k+1)−1), the finite geometric sum. After a cap is reached,
each further full-window wait adds c. For the original eight windows,
these offsets are 1,3,7,15,31,61,91,121.

Under ideal independent full jitter, the expected cumulative idle wait is
one half the sum of windows, and its variance is the sum of W_j²/12.
That halves the expected idle budget relative to full windows in this
specific calculation. It does not halve RPC latency, which would also
depend on execution times, success rates, queueing and retry policy.
A cap bounds each window; an infinite sequence of retries can still have
unbounded total idle wait. No retry-count limit or aggregate rate limit
is supplied by the scalar window itself.

The next controlled fixture draws two thousand distinct seeded schedules.
The native half-window schedule gives the ideal mean curve exactly for
these representable numbers. Empirical means and sample standard deviations
are computed from actual cumulative offsets, not reconstructed codewords
or a simulation of successful requests.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/backoff_offsets.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto full=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_schedule(12,1,30),half=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_schedule(12,1,30,std::vector<double>(12,.5));dm::random::SplitMix64 seeds(20150304);
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> offsets(12);for(int client=0;client<2000;++client){const auto s=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_seeded(12,1,30,seeds.uniform_u64(1,std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max()));for(std::size_t j=0;j<s.retry_times.size();++j)offsets[j].push_back(s.retry_times[j]);}
  std::vector<double>x,means;double variance=0;std::print("| k | window | full-window offset | ideal jitter mean | ideal jitter SD | actual mean | actual sample SD |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<12;++i){const dm::Vector<> values(offsets[i]);variance+=full.steps[i].window*full.steps[i].window/12.;const auto mean=dm::mean(values);std::print("| {} | {:.0f} | {:.0f} | {:.2f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",i,full.steps[i].window,full.retry_times[i],half.retry_times[i],std::sqrt(variance),mean,dm::sd(values));x.push_back(i);means.push_back(mean);if(half.retry_times[i]!=.5*full.retry_times[i])throw std::runtime_error("half-window mean identity failed");}
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.line(x,full.retry_times,"Full windows",{37,99,235},2).line(x,half.retry_times,"Ideal jitter mean",{124,58,237},2).points(x,means,"Sample mean N=2000",{22,163,74},5)
    .title("Cumulative idle waiting: exact reference and sampled mean").x_label("Last included zero-based wait k").y_label("Sum of idle waits (request time excluded)").size(1000,540).save_svg("build/backoff_offsets.svg");
}
