> Finite limits, rejected inputs and the scope of the calculation

The original loop multiplied by two until the cap was met. For zero base
and positive cap, it still iterated k times even though the answer was
always zero. Near the largest double it could raise floating overflow in
an intermediate product and then return a finite cap. The new comparison
kernel avoids both behaviours. Its fixed-operation claim concerns the
algorithm on fixed-width scalars, rather than a benchmark or clock deadline.

Negative indices/counts, nonfinite or negative base/cap, and nonfinite or
out-of-range explicit u are rejected, including parameter checks for an empty
sequence. A zero seed is refused because the xorshift state would remain
zero. These replace malformed-input behaviours; the valid legacy outputs
and the inclusive u=1 endpoint are retained.

A pure vector of finite windows can be valid even when their cumulative
sum cannot fit. Native schedules reject a delay greater than the remaining
finite capacity DBL_MAX−total before adding it. They return no partial
schedule. They still use ordinary floating summation, so tiny increments
can be rounded away. There is no artificial capture quota for this intrinsic
O(N) output. Windows, steps and offsets are independently owned values.

This application full-jitter calculation is distinct from TCP's prescribed
retransmission timer. RFC 6298 section 5.5 doubles its RTO after timeout and
section 2.5 constrains any cap; this report implements neither that complete
timer nor Ethernet's discrete collision-slot protocol.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/backoff_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto max=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();const auto zero=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_step(std::numeric_limits<int>::max(),0,30),cap=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_step(1,.75*max,max),small=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_step(std::numeric_limits<int>::max(),std::numeric_limits<double>::denorm_min(),max);
  std::print("Huge index/zero base: window {:.0f}; capped {}; scaled {}. Near-maximum doubling: finite {}; equals cap {}; scaled {}. Smallest positive base/huge index: equals cap {}; scaled {}.\n",zero.window,zero.capped,zero.scaled,std::isfinite(cap.window),cap.window==max,cap.scaled,small.window==max,small.scaled);
  int invalid=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_delay(-1,1,30);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_sequence(-1,1,30);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_sequence(0,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),30);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_jittered(1,1,30,2);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_seeded(0,1,30,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}
  const auto windows=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_sequence(2,max,max);bool overflow=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_schedule(2,max,max);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow=true;}
  const auto representable=dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_schedule(2,max,max,{.5,.5});std::print("Invalid-parameter rejections {}/5; valid maximum windows {}; their full-wait sum rejected {}; half-wait sum equals maximum {}.\n",invalid,windows.size(),overflow,representable.total_delay==max);
  std::print("Legacy jitter endpoint u=1: {:.0f}; valid empty windows {}; valid empty seeded steps {}.\n",dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_jittered(3,1,30,1),dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_sequence(0,1,30).size(),dm::algorithms::exponential_backoff_seeded(0,1,30).steps.size());
  if(invalid!=5||!overflow||!cap.capped||small.scaled||zero.scaled)throw std::runtime_error("finite/domain control failed");
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.8;box.height=2;box.font_size=22;box.fill={191,219,254};
  g.node("zero",{0,0},std::format("k = INT_MAX, base = 0\nwindow {:.0f}\nldexp used {}",zero.window,zero.scaled),box);box.fill={254,215,170};
  g.node("cap",{6.5,0},std::format("base = .75 * DBL_MAX\nfinite cap returned {}\nldexp used {}",cap.capped,cap.scaled),box);box.fill={187,247,208};
  g.node("sum",{13,0},std::format("Two maximum windows\nordinary output valid {}\nfull-wait sum rejected {}",windows.size()==2,overflow),box)
    .text({6.5,3},"Checked numeric results; no sleeping or network request",26).save_svg("build/backoff_limits.svg");
}
